T00:19:34Z","closed_at":"2026-10-06T00:19:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124132","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124132","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124132.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124132.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-06T00:19:23Z"},"body":"**What problem(s) does this PR solve?**\r\nOmniLight3D and SpotLight3D soft shadows are broken on the Mobile renderer (forward_mobile). With light_size above zero, shadows completely disappear at default soft shadow quality (Soft Low) as well as Hard, Soft Very Low, and Soft Medium. At High and Ultra the edges look rough, and with light_size set to zero they use the wrong sample count.\r\nThis is a regression introduced in #112178 (merged September 21, 2026). The C++ side packs positional light sample counts at bit 20 and 26, but the shader was updated to read them from bit 24 and 30 instead.\r\nFixes the bit offsets in scene_forward_mobile_inc.glsl so they match C++ again.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Additional information**\r\n4.7 is not affected as this only exists in 4.8 dev builds.\r\nTested on macOS (Metal, M3 Pro) across all soft shadow quality settings. Mobile shadow output now matches Forward+ for both light_size 0.5 and 0.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2070\" height=\"840\" alt=\"light_size_0 5\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f83fac14-0b70-46d2-8d5a-a733da686ed4\" />\r\n<img width=\"2070\" height=\"840\" alt=\"light_size_0\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d705d07d-b19d-455a-9556-50c17d005bd7\" />\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124132/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124132/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}